{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestSimplePaths"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"DirectedGraph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Distance"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each path is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Path","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with the edges it takes, paired with its length. Paths are told apart by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"their edges, so parallel edges give distinct paths. Paths of equal length come in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unspecified order. The out-edges and their weights are copied when the sequence is made; each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"path after the first then costs up to one shortest-path search per vertex on the path before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. Taking a prefix, ","type":"text"},{"code":"prefix(k)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", gives the k shortest simple paths.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each iterator starts over from the first path. Holds a copy of the graph, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPathTree"},{"type":"text","text":" does."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths0a6SimpleB0V","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ShortestSimplePaths"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","title":"ShortestSimplePaths","remoteSource":{"fileName":"ShortestSimplePaths.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths.swift#L326"},"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ShortestSimplePaths","kind":"identifier"}]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/shortestsimplepaths"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The simple paths from a source to a target in order of length, shortest first, listed lazily"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by Yen’s algorithm with Lawler’s refinement."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/ST"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/ShortestSimplePaths\/Iterator"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Shor